  "plan": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "action": "Make two facing pages the working recovery target, preserving current body type, hero/circle/sticker, diagrams and approved Growing guide · crop navigation. Keep frozen originals and canonical records intact; do not silently publish a third page when the target fails."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "action": "Pilot carrot and onions/shallots. Restore measured choice of logical practical-column arrangements at compact width; optimise spacing and block placement across the spread before changing prose."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "action": "Prepare source-linked compact editorial drafts for residual shortages. Tighten repeated sentences and measurements and repeated Key risks/pest-table explanations. Keep seed and set routes, crop-specific timings, safety and useful controls. Any proposed transfer to the Troubles section must point to an existing page that names the vegetable and retains the actual advice; record any omissions for John. Do not enforce a fixed pest-row or variety quota."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "action": "Show the two pilot spreads in actual metric and imperial PDFs with changes highlighted. Onions is the harder case: balancing alone leaves substantial excess. Do not promise every current sentence fits unchanged."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
